{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["נשני — from נשש. Like חנני אלהים from חנן. The dagesh is in place of the missing letter. And had it been from the pattern of לא תנשני, נשיתי טובה, which is from the clipped למ\"ד פעל form, it should have been נשני, like עבדי רמני, האיש אשר כלני — רמני from רימה את רעהו; כלנו — כלה ה׳ את חמתו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The logic appears to be: since נשני has a dagesh compensating for a missing letter, it cannot be from the למ\"ד פעל pattern (which would also yield נשני but without needing a dagesh); therefore it must be from the root נשש with assimilation. Translated hyper-literally; the syntax of the original is compressed and the argument's steps are inferred from the forms cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:03.769284785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}